[[!meta title="Sound and video"]]

Tails includes several sound and video applications:

  - [*Audacity*](https://www.audacityteam.org/), a multi-track audio editor.

    See the [official documentation](http://manual.audacityteam.org/).

  - [*Brasero*](https://wiki.gnome.org/Apps/Brasero), an application to
    burn, copy, and erase CDs and DVDs.

  - [*Sound Juicer*](https://wiki.gnome.org/Apps/SoundJuicer), a CD
    ripper application.

  - [*Sound Recorder*](https://wiki.gnome.org/Apps/SoundRecorder), a sound recorder.

  - [*Celluloid*](https://celluloid-player.github.io/), an audio and video player.

    <div class="bug">

    <p>For added security, <i>Celluloid</i> cannot access the network. You can
    either:</p>

    <ul>

      <li>Open online videos, like MP4 and AVI files, in <i>Tor Browser</i>.

      <li>Open online streaming addresses, like IPTV and HLS addresses, in
      <i>VLC</i>, installed as [[additional
      software|persistent_storage/additional_software]].</li>

      <!-- Test URLs:

      - https://test-streams.mux.dev/x36xhzz/x36xhzz.m3u8
      - https://tails.net/install/inc/videos/mac.mp4

      -->

    </ul>

    </div>

    <div class="bug">

    <p><i>Celluloid</i> doesn't work on some computers from 2011 or earlier.</p>

    <p>You can use <i>VLC</i> instead, installed as [[additional
    software|persistent_storage/additional_software]].</p>

    </div>

These applications are available in the **Apps&nbsp;▸ Sound & Video** submenu.

You can also install using the [[Additional Software|persistent_storage/additional_software]] feature:

- [*VLC*](https://www.videolan.org/vlc/), a multimedia player with advanced
  features.

- [*Pitivi*](https://www.pitivi.org/), a video editor.

- [*GNOME Camera*](https://apps.gnome.org/Snapshot/), from the `gnome-snapshot` package, an application
  to take pictures and videos from your webcam.

